  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Locally Driven Clean Energy Initiative in Binga District, Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will focus on clean energy options for communities in Binga district in Zimbabwe who usually depend on fire wood as their main source of energy. This practice is continuously degrading the environment and natural resources are continually being depleted. Main outcomes of the project will be i) Increased adoption of clean energy technologies, ii) Empowered women, youths and people with disabilities drive the adoption of clean energy technologies, iii) Communities have strengthened by-laws for natural resource management (NRM). energy options that are not currently being used in the district and are going to be introduced by the project will be biogas at institutional and household level and solar for lighting.</narrative>
  </description>
